$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-(3-Nitrophenyl)-6-(pyrrolidin-1-yl)pyridine (30). To a solution of 29
(2 g, 8.81 mmol) and 3-nitrophenylboronic acid (1.62 g, 9.69 mmol) in
1,2-dimethoxyethane (10 mL) were added Ba(OH)2 (3.32 g, 19.37 mmol) and
water (4 mL) under argon atmosphere. The contents were degassed,
Pd(Ph3P)4 (0.305 g, 0.26 mmol) was added, and the resulting mixture was
irradiated with microwaves at 150 °C for 15 min. It was then diluted with
200 mL of ethyl acetate and water (1:1), and the organic layer was
separated, washed with water and brine, and dried over MgSO4. Volatiles
were concentrated under reduced pressure to give crude product which was
purified by silica gel chromatography (20-70%; EtOAc:hexanes). 30 (2.05
g, 86% yield) as a yellow solid. 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d 6) δ: 8.57 (t, J
= 1.5 Hz, 1H), 8.50 (td, J = 8.0 Hz, J = 1.5 Hz, 1H), 8.23 (ddd, J = 8.0
Hz, J = 2.5 Hz, J = 1.0 Hz, 1H), 7.74 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.63 (dd, J =
8.0 Hz, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 7.28 (d, J = 7.0 Hz, 1H), 6.51 (d, J = 8.0 Hz,
1H), 3.49 (t, J = 6.5 Hz, 4H), 2.04-1.94 (quin, J = 3.0 Hz, 4H). Mass
spectrum m/z 270.1 [M + H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, thermal, Suzuki coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Novel Electrophilic and Photoaffinity Covalent Probes for Mapping the
Cannabinoid 1 Receptor Allosteric Site(s)
