$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 2-Aminobiphenyls 1. Synthesis of 1b is representative. To
a 20 mL two-necked flask with a reflux condenser, a balloon, and a rubber
cup were added 2-bromoaniline (2 mmol, 344 mg), 4-methylphenylboronic
acid (3 mmol, 408 mg), PdCl2(PPh3)2 (0.2 mmol, 140 mg), K2CO3 (3 mmol,
415 mg) and DMF/H2O (10/2 mL). Then, the resulting mixture was stirred
under nitrogen at 80 °C for 24 h. After cooling, the reaction mixture was
diluted with ethyl acetate (20 mL) and insoluble solids were filtered off
through a short pad of celite. The organic layer was washed by aqueous
NaHCO3 (100 mL, three times), and dried over Na2SO4. Volatiles were
removed in vacuo and subsequent purification by column chromatography on
silica gel using hexane-ethyl acetate (10:1, v/v) as eluent. Amine 1b
(309 mg, 1.69 mmol) in 84% yield.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Direct Synthesis of N-H Carbazoles via Iridium(III)-Catalyzed
Intramolecular C-H Amination
