$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure (2) for the Synthesis of
Phenyl-Substituted Benzoxazolone Intermediates 39a-g and
Alkenyl-Substituted Intermediates 40a-b. The appropriate
bromo-substituted 3H-1,3-benzoxazol-2-one (1.0 equiv) was suspended in a
1:1 toluene/EtOH mixture (10 mL per mmol benzoxazolone). The boronic acid
(1.5 equiv) was added followed by aq Na2CO3 (2 M, 0.55 mL per mmol
benzoxazolone, 1.1 equiv). The resulting suspension was degassed under
nitrogen for 10 min, followed by addition of tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)
palladium(0) (0.1 equiv) and heating under microwave irradiation at 100
°C for 30 min. The reaction mixture was diluted with EtOAc (40 mL per
mmol benzoxazolone), and water (40 mL per mmol benzoxazolone) was added.
The two phases were separated and the aqueous layer was extracted with
EtOAc (2 × 40 mL per mmol benzoxazolone). The combined organic phases
were dried over Na2SO4, evaporated on celite or silica, and the compound
was purified by silica gel column chromatography using the Teledyne ISCO
apparatus (cyclohexane/EtOAc, unless otherwise stated).
4-Phenyl-3H-1,3-benzoxazol-2-one (39a). The reaction was carried out
following the general procedure (2), starting from 4-bromobenzoxazolone
(37a, 160 mg, 0.748 mmol) and phenylboronic acid (137 mg, 1.12 mmol). In
total, three microwave cycles were applied using fresh palladium catalyst
and boronic acid each time. Compound was obtained as a white solid after
two purifications by column chromatography, but still only in low purity
(~70% by UPLC and NMR; impurities were triphenylphosphine oxide and
4-bromobenzoxazolone). 6-[(E)-Styryl]-3H-1,3-benzoxazol-2-one (40a). The
reaction was carried out following the general procedure (2), starting
from 6-bromobenzoxazolone (160 mg, 0.750 mmol) and [(E)-styryl]boronic
acid (166 mg, 1.12 mmol). White solid (131.2 mg, 74%). 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.03 (d, J = 8.1 Hz, 1H), 7.07 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 7.26 - 7.31
(m, 3H), 7.32 - 7.44 (m, 3H), 7.47 - 7.53 (m, 2H), 7.98 (s, 1H). MS (ESI)
m/z: 236 [M - H]-.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki-Miyaura reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
